That I'd like to see. If I only loot Minetown, a Healer is more than
safe enough (but not more than any other gnome or a decently equipped
wizard). If I go further, he (or his pet) will run out of food.

BTW, I used to be a healer specialist, too. I would have a 100%
success at PR with a gnomish healer (I guess that I still would do
it). I would lost it in the midgame or endgame, for some YASD.
Eventually, I learned that the protection racket with a gnomish healer
was almost a conduct compared to a knight or tourist. I started with a
Knight, and gave up after some failed quests. Then I tried tourist,
and guess what- YAFAP with the 10th tourist or so.

In the endgame, healers suck a lot. They only have the Staff, which is
superb, but if someone steals it (and someone will), you are screwed,
you have no comparable backup. Compare it to a tourist, that can have
his PYEC into a bag until he needs it. Or to a knight, that *averages*
96 damage with his magic missiles, combined with pounding+jousting.


